just the other day samsung accidentally  leaked their upcoming flagship galaxy  tab s8 ultra tablet on their own website  and if that wasn't bad enough it  apparently comes with a notch yes a  notch and i don't know if you remember  or not but samsung has been making fun  of apple's notch for years ever since  the iphone 10 and even as recent as last  year when they made fun of the new  macbook pros notch but thanks to these  new leaked images it's pretty clear that  samsung was ironically working on a  notched tablet of their own the entire  time and if you think it couldn't get  any worse they actually leak the specs  of each of the different tab sa models  by posting actual listings to amazon  with official images of each model and  the folks over at android authority were  nice enough to compile a chart with all  of the specs and to be completely honest  if these are the actual specs that these  tablets will come with then i think  there's a pretty good chance that the  tab s8 ultra is gonna fail at least  compared to apple's m1 ipad pro which is  soon going to be a full year old not to  mention their upcoming m2 ipad pro  coming later this year so in this video  i'm going to be comparing the leak specs  and features of the tap sa ultra to what  we already have with the m1 ipad pro to  show how samsung's new tablet is more  behind than ever before now the first  thing i want to mention is that there is  going to be three different sizes  including an 11 inch lcd model a 12.7  inch amoled model and finally the new  14.6 inch ultra which is the one that's  coming with the notch and the reason for  that is because it apparently comes with  a secondary 12 megapixel selfie camera  which probably uses an ultra wide lens  and looking at the official product  images that samsung leaked on amazon the  tab s8 and s8 plus look essentially  identical to the design of the previous  tab s7 which we already compared to the  m1 ipad pro and since the leaked display  specs on the new tab s8 plus model is  literally identical to the one in the  tab s7 plus i'll actually be able to  show you guys the differences in display  quality from our previous comparison  video but before we get into all of that  i want to compare some of the other  specs that were leaked especially the  new chip unlike last year every tab is 8  model will now come with 8 gigs of ram  which perfectly matches up to both  models of the ipad pro and the ultra  model will now be able to come with up  to 16 gigs just like the m1 can and now  as far as the storage space both the  regular and plus models will come with  128 gigs of base storage just like the  ipad pro except that the ultra model  will now come with  256 gigs at the base price which is  actually pretty nice however the leaked  amazon listing showed a price of around  13.08 euros for the 5g model which  converts to around 14.79 usd  which is actually more expensive than a  similarly spec 12.9 inch ipad pro with  256 gigs of storage and 5g cellular  supports but keep in mind that the tab  sa ultra will have a larger 14.6 inch  display so i guess the big question is  if you're gonna be paying more money for  a samsung android tablet than an ipad  pro  what benefits are you getting other than  the larger display size well first of  all the s pen is going to be included  compared to having to buy the apple  pencil separately for the ipad but  unfortunately it's been confirmed that  samsung has not upgraded the s pen at  all since the last generation another  benefit is that the battery size on the  tab s8 ultra will be around four percent  larger than the one that's in the 12.9  inch ipad pro and one more advantage  that i really wish the m1 ipad pro had  is the latest bluetooth 5.2 and wi-fi 6e  supports on all of the tab s8 models  which should be a nice bonus and then as  far as the cameras it's a hit or miss  because the ultra comes with two selfie  cameras both packed with 12 megapixel  sensors which is going to be nice for  both close-up shots and ultra wide but  then when you get to the rear the  ultrawide camera only has 6 megapixel  resolution compared to 12 on the ipad  pro but at least the main camera has 13  megapixels on the rear instead of 12 on  the ipad but now getting into the major  downsides of these new tap s8 tablets  the usbc ports only support usb 3.2 gen  1 speeds which means transfer speeds of  only 5 gigabits per second compared to  the m1 ipad pro which comes with a  thunderbolt port with speeds up to 40  gigabits per second which is 8 times  faster so that's already something that  should get potential buyers thinking  since the ipad pro has such a huge  advantage in terms of the port but going  further every new tab s8 model including  the ultra is coming with the same  snapdragon 8 gen 1 chip which let me  remind you is a smartphone chip and if  you're wondering how powerful this chip  is compared to apple's m1 and the ipad  pro let me first show you how it  compares to apple's lower end iphone  chips and this brings us to a snapdragon  8 gen 1 chip review video from geekerwan  who according to the title  don't think too fondly of this new chip  compared to the previous snapdragon 888  the new chip is only 1.5 faster in terms  of geekbench 5 multi-core performance  and only around 5.7 faster for single  core and the crazy thing about it is  that it's slower than the three year old  a13 chip from the iphone 11. yes let me  repeat that the brand new snapdragon 8  gen 1 going into the new flagship galaxy  tab s8 ultra has less single core  performance than the iphone 11's a13  channel but to make things even worse  this new snapdragon chip consumes  considerably more power than apple's a14  and a15 chips while being a lot slower  as you can see on the right side where  it shows the score per watt and in case  you're wondering how it compares to the  m1 chip within the eight month old ipad  pro the m1 is about 42.5 faster in terms  of single core and literally almost  twice as fast in terms of multi-core but  thankfully things over on the graphics  side are a little bit better since the  snapdragon's gpu actually compared to  the lower end version of the new a15  when using the vulkan api which is  pretty impressive however looking at the  power consumption it uses 72 percent  more power than that same four core a15  ship leading to a pretty terrible  performance per watt score but then once  again when we compare it to the m1 ipad  pro there is a massive difference with  the m1 scoring 82 fps in the 1440p test  and 210 in the 1080p test making it 60  to 70 faster than the snapdragon 8 gen  1. so as you guys can see the upcoming  galaxy tab s8 ultra is no match for  apple's m1 ipad pro especially in the  multi-core performance department but  now the last saving grace for the  samsung tablet is the amoled display so  let's revisit our comparison of the tab  s7 plus and the 12.9 inch m1 ipad pro  one of the downsides of samsung's  display is that it's very reflective so  it causes it to look great instead of  being a very deep and dark black like on  the ipad pro and when you're holding it  up to your and what and when you're  holding it and when you're holding it up  to your face the samsung display almost  looks like a mirror compared to barely  anything being visible on the ipad and  then in terms of hdr brightness the mini  led display on the ipad pro looks  incredibly bright compared to the gray  looking samsung however the mini led  tech did suffer from blooming in this  fireworks scene compared to amoled that  looks much better with no blooming at  all so there's a point for the samsung  tablet but with all that said the specs  of the new tab s8 just can't compare  with the m1 ipad pro especially in terms  of performance and usbc port speeds and  that's even before we get into the  differences in resale value reliability  and the app store and this was honestly  the year where samsung needed to show a  huge improvement in order to catch up to  apple's m1 ipad pro but in my opinion  they have failed and this is all really  bad news for when apple releases their  m2 ipad pro later this year which will  take it up another notch so if you're  interested in seeing samsung's new  tablet go heads ahead with apple's m1  ipad pro here in the next few weeks  click that circle above to subscribe for  more videos like this one and check out  one of those two videos right over there  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next video  [Music]
 

